### Banking API requests for IntelliJ's built-in HTTP client.
### Start the API first (run BankingApiApp), then click the green arrow next to a request.
### Run them top to bottom: login saves the token, and the later requests use it.

### Health check
GET http://localhost:8080/api/health

### Register alice
POST http://localhost:8080/api/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice",
  "fullName": "Alice Doe",
  "password": "Passw0rd1"
}

### Register bob (the second account to transfer to)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "bob",
  "fullName": "Bob Roe",
  "password": "Passw0rd1"
}

### Log in as alice (saves the token for the requests below)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice",
  "password": "Passw0rd1"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("token", response.body.token);
%}

### My account
GET http://localhost:8080/api/account
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Deposit
POST http://localhost:8080/api/deposit
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 250.75
}

### Withdraw
POST http://localhost:8080/api/withdraw
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 20
}

### Transfer to bob (bob's account number is shown when you register him)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/transfer
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "toAccountNumber": "1000000002",
  "amount": 50
}

### Transaction history
GET http://localhost:8080/api/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Log out (the token stops working)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}
